---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../utils/paths';

const snippet = `curl -fsSL https://krabka.io/quickstart/docker-compose.yml -o docker-compose.yml && docker compose up -d`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Introduction"
  description="Documentation for the krabka Kafka-compatible broker, KRaft metadata quorum, clients, stream processing libraries, connectors, and Kubernetes operator."
  currentSlug="/docs"
>
  <div class="space-y-6 font-sans">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">krabka Documentation</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-sm max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        Guides for building, operating, and streaming with krabka.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <strong class="text-white">krabka</strong> implements the Apache Kafka wire protocol and <a href={getPath('/features/kraft')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">KRaft metadata quorum</a> in Rust. The broker forbids <a href={getPath('/verification#memory-safety')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300"><code class="font-mono text-krab-300">unsafe</code> code</a>. <a href="https://creusot.rs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">Creusot</a> proves selected decision-kernel contracts, and <a href="https://www.stateright.rs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">Stateright</a> checks failure sequences within model bounds. The <a href={getPath('/docs/kip-matrix')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">compatibility matrix</a> lists API support and implementation status.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Components</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Byte-exact wire parity:</strong> Codecs generated directly from upstream Apache Kafka JSON schemas. Compatible with standard <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">kafka-clients</code>, JVM CLI tools, and existing producer/consumer applications.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white"><a href={getPath('/features/kraft')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">Native KRaft quorum:</a></strong> Metadata is replicated via a native Raft implementation (<code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-raft</code>) implementing the KIP-595 RPC protocol with zero ZooKeeper dependency.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white"><a href={getPath('/features/tiered-storage')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">Tiered storage subsystem:</a></strong> Asynchronously offloads sealed partition segments to Amazon S3-compatible stores (including MinIO) or Google Cloud Storage (KIP-405).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white"><a href={getPath('/features/streams')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">Stream processing:</a></strong> Libraries for Go, Java, and Rust with state stores, <a href="https://arrow.apache.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">Apache Arrow</a> batch operators, <a href={getPath('/docs/data-formats')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-krab-300">schema serdes</a>, and barrier coordination. Support varies by language.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Correctness & Verification</h2>
      <p>
        See <a href={getPath('/verification')} class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 font-semibold underline">Correctness & Verification</a> for how safe Rust, Creusot proofs, Stateright model checking, mutation testing, and differential suites fit together, and the <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/verification')} class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 font-semibold underline">verification catalog</a> for every proof, every model, and the formal boundary.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Architectural Deep Dives</h2>
      <p>
        For engineering rationale and system topology:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          <a href={getPath('/docs/architecture')} class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 font-semibold underline">Ecosystem Architecture:</a> Repository boundaries and one-way dependency layering from the wire codecs up to the operator.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={getPath('/docs/runtime-architecture')} class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 font-semibold underline">Runtime Architecture:</a> Operational topology, control plane reconcile loops, and data plane interactions between broker nodes, schema registry, and operator.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">The Broader krabka Ecosystem</h2>
      <p>
        This site covers the broker and the Kafka ecosystem around it. Projects that build on the broker but are not Kafka components are documented in their own repositories: <a href="https://github.com/krabka-io/krabka-o11y" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 font-semibold underline">krabka-o11y</a> for observability and <a href="https://github.com/krabka-io/gres" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 font-semibold underline">gres</a> for Postgres-compatible compute on krabka.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Continuous Documentation Pipeline</h2>
      <p>
        The krabka documentation hub is decoupled from individual sub-repositories and synchronized automatically:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Decentralized authoring:</strong> Architecture and engineering guides are maintained directly alongside the code in each component repository (<code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-broker</code>, <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-streams-java</code>, and <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-streams-go</code>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">API references:</strong> Each component repository builds and publishes its own Rustdoc, Javadoc, or Go reference. The <a href={getPath('/api')} class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 font-semibold underline">/api</a> directory links to those sites.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Build synchronization:</strong> The site build imports Markdown guides from the broker, Java streams, and Go streams repositories.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Quick Run</h2>
      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span>Start local single-node broker:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-colors text-xs" data-copy={snippet}>
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <CodeBlock code={snippet} lang="bash" />
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Next Steps</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose pt-1">
        <a href={getPath('/docs/quickstart')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Quickstart Guide →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Spin up a local broker cluster with Docker Compose or deploy to Kubernetes via Helm.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={getPath('/docs/architecture')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Ecosystem Architecture →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Explore repository dependency layering, crate boundaries, and wire-protocol modularity.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
